    "result_text": "The full suite is green. There's only one runnable test (`AcceptanceTest`; the other two files are a base class and a helper), and it passes.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe change makes owner creation return a `displayName` formatted as `LastName, FirstName`. The test creates an owner via `POST /api/owners` and reads it back via `GET /api/owners/{id}`, asserting `$.displayName == \"LastName, FirstName\"`.\n\nTwo edits implement this:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `displayName` string property to the `Owner` schema, so the OpenAPI-generated `OwnerDto` gains a `displayName` field.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../model/Owner.java`** \u2014 added a `getDisplayName()` method returning `getLastName() + \", \" + getFirstName()`. MapStruct's `toOwnerDto` mapping picks this up automatically (matching source getter \u2192 target `displayName`), so the value is populated from the stored names on every read.\n\nBecause `displayName` is derived from the stored `firstName`/`lastName` at mapping time, it's correct for both the create response and subsequent GETs, and it's marked `readOnly` so it can't be supplied on input. `mvnw test` \u2192 `BUILD SUCCESS`, `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`.",
